($q$CALC_201$q$, $q$Terminal Weighted Moving Average$q$, $q$Terminal indicator I03 (Weighted Moving Average), as the terminal charts compute it. Convention source: TA_LIB; TA-Lib equivalent: WMA; related: CALC_023. HTML engine equals TA-Lib.$q$, $q$asset_id;date;close$q$, $q$WMA=SUM((n-i)*src[t-i], i=0..n-1)/(n(n+1)/2). Inputs are final daily bars of one ticker in ascending date order (no gaps filled, no zero-filled prehistory). EMA-type averages are seeded with the SMA of their first n valid values; RMA uses alpha 1/n with the same seed. A value is null until its window is full; a zero denominator gives null unless the convention says otherwise. Calculations use the full stored history (price files from 2018) so recursive values match Feature 04.$q$, $q$length=20; source=close$q$, $q$wma$q$, $q$Terminal TS calc module key wma (I03); verification/terminal_api/INDICATOR_SPEC.md$q$),
($q$CALC_202$q$, $q$Terminal Hull Moving Average$q$, $q$Terminal indicator I04 (Hull Moving Average), as the terminal charts compute it. Convention source: HTML; no TA-Lib function. No TA-Lib function; lengths are floored.$q$, $q$asset_id;date;close$q$, $q$HMA=WMA(2*WMA(src,floor(n/2))-WMA(src,n), floor(sqrt(n))); each length at least 1. Inputs are final daily bars of one ticker in ascending date order (no gaps filled, no zero-filled prehistory). EMA-type averages are seeded with the SMA of their first n valid values; RMA uses alpha 1/n with the same seed. A value is null until its window is full; a zero denominator gives null unless the convention says otherwise. Calculations use the full stored history (price files from 2018) so recursive values match Feature 04.$q$, $q$length=9; source=close$q$, $q$hma$q$, $q$Terminal TS calc module key hma (I04); verification/terminal_api/INDICATOR_SPEC.md$q$),
($q$CALC_203$q$, $q$Terminal Kaufman Adaptive Moving Average$q$, $q$Terminal indicator I05 (Kaufman Adaptive Moving Average), as the terminal charts compute it. Convention source: TA_LIB; TA-Lib equivalent: KAMA. Equals TA-Lib KAMA at fast=2, slow=30 (TA-Lib fixes them; other values follow the same formula).$q$, $q$asset_id;date;close$q$, $q$ER=ABS(src[t]-src[t-n])/SUM(ABS(src[j]-src[j-1]),n); SC=(ER*(2/(fast+1)-2/(slow+1))+2/(slow+1))^2; KAMA[t]=KAMA[t-1]+SC*(src[t]-KAMA[t-1]); first KAMA seeded with src[n-1]. Inputs are final daily bars of one ticker in ascending date order (no gaps filled, no zero-filled prehistory). EMA-type averages are seeded with the SMA of their first n valid values; RMA uses alpha 1/n with the same seed. A value is null until its window is full; a zero denominator gives null unless the convention says otherwise. Calculations use the full stored history (price files from 2018) so recursive values match Feature 04.$q$, $q$length=10; fast_length=2; slow_length=30; source=close$q$, $q$kama$q$, $q$Terminal TS calc module key kama (I05); verification/terminal_api/INDICATOR_SPEC.md$q$),
($q$CALC_204$q$, $q$Terminal Aroon$q$, $q$Terminal indicator I08 (Aroon), as the terminal charts compute it. Convention source: TA_LIB; TA-Lib equivalent: AROON. HTML engine equals TA-Lib.$q$, $q$asset_id;date;high;low$q$, $q$AroonUp=100*(n-bars since highest high in the last n+1 bars)/n; AroonDown likewise with the lowest low; ties take the most recent bar. Inputs are final daily bars of one ticker in ascending date order (no gaps filled, no zero-filled prehistory). EMA-type averages are seeded with the SMA of their first n valid values; RMA uses alpha 1/n with the same seed. A value is null until its window is full; a zero denominator gives null unless the convention says otherwise. Calculations use the full stored history (price files from 2018) so recursive values match Feature 04.$q$, $q$length=14$q$, $q$aroon_up, aroon_down$q$, $q$Terminal TS calc module key aroon (I08); verification/terminal_api/INDICATOR_SPEC.md$q$),
($q$CALC_205$q$, $q$Terminal Supertrend$q$, $q$Terminal indicator I09 (Supertrend), as the terminal charts compute it. Convention source: HTML; no TA-Lib function. Uses the TA-Lib ATR of I30.$q$, $q$asset_id;date;high;low;close$q$, $q$basic bands=HL2±factor*ATR(atr_length) (ATR as I30); final upper band keeps the lower of basic and previous unless the previous close was above it (lower band mirrored); direction flips when close crosses the active band. Inputs are final daily bars of one ticker in ascending date order (no gaps filled, no zero-filled prehistory). EMA-type averages are seeded with the SMA of their first n valid values; RMA uses alpha 1/n with the same seed. A value is null until its window is full; a zero denominator gives null unless the convention says otherwise. Calculations use the full stored history (price files from 2018) so recursive values match Feature 04.$q$, $q$atr_length=10; factor=3$q$, $q$supertrend, direction$q$, $q$Terminal TS calc module key supertrend (I09); verification/terminal_api/INDICATOR_SPEC.md$q$),
